WEBVTT

NOTE English translation; original display timings, not word alignment.

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.930
Hi, I'm VoiceStudio's demo voice.

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.310
Welcome!

3
00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:07.500
The new line was generated
using the first voice sample.

4
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.667
This open-source project
is called VoiceStudio.

5
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.833
Its speech models can run
on your own device.

6
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.533
It puts different speech engines
in one interface.

7
00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:19.233
Choose an engine.

8
00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:21.900
The backend sends the job
to its model.

9
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.933
That example used OmniVoice.

10
00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:28.000
It uses the reference recording
and that recording's transcript

11
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.033
to speak the new line.

12
00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:34.467
Say a game adds a new plot twist
and needs another line of dialogue.

13
00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:38.900
Use an old recording you have rights to,
and generate a version to listen to.

14
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.100
Repository link in the comments.
